 "recommendation": "DO NOT SHIP the star-shrinkage formula. Variant A (stars only) is a statistical tie with raw out-of-sample (Brier 0.1501 vs 0.1501, per-timepoint diffs <=0.0002 = noise). Variants B/C (n-penalties) are clearly worse (+0.0010 OOS). The tree's MIN_N=20 gate + backoff lookup already handles thin-data uncertainty; extra shrinkage is redundant. HOWEVER: calibration shows the raw tree is 2-5pp overconfident above 60% and 1-2pp underconfident below 30%. Shrinking toward TRUNK cannot fix this because the trunk shares the bias. The correct follow-up is shrinkage toward the global base rate (~33%) or post-hoc recalibration (Platt/isotonic) -- a different experiment."
